  "text": "### Common Customer Questions  \n**Q: Can my interest rate go down?**\nA: Yes, if the Bank of England base rate falls. Your rate always stays 2.5% above BoE.  \n**Q: Will my interest ever be locked in?**\nA: No, SmartSaver is always variable. If you want a fixed rate, ask about our Fixed Rate Bonds (coming 2026).  \n**Q: What if I withdraw money — do I lose interest?**\nA: No, you earn interest on your balance every day. If you withdraw on day 15, you earn interest for the first 15 days that month.  \n**Q: Can I have multiple SmartSaver accounts?**\nA: No, one account per customer. But you can have a SmartSaver AND a Current Account if you want.  \n**Q: Is there a notice period to access my money?**\nA: No, it's fully accessible. Withdraw anytime by online banking, ATM, or visiting a branch.",
